</span>
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span><span id="id10" class="ltx_text">New York, USA</span>
</span></span></span></span></div>

<div id="abstract1" class="ltx_abstract"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_abstract">Abstract</h6>
    
<p id="abstract1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="abstract1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Disentangled and interpretable latent representations in generative models typically come at the cost of generation quality. The </span><math id="abstract1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="abstract1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">-VAE framework introduces a hyperparameter </span><math id="abstract1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="abstract1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to balance disentanglement and reconstruction quality, where setting </span><math id="abstract1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="abstract1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> introduces an information bottleneck that favors disentanglement over sharp, accurate reconstructions. To address this trade-off, we propose a novel generative modeling framework that leverages a range of </span><math id="abstract1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="abstract1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> values to learn multiple corresponding latent representations. First, we obtain a slew of representations by training a single variational autoencoder (VAE), with a new loss function that controls the information retained in each latent representation such that the higher </span><math id="abstract1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="abstract1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> value prioritize disentanglement over reconstruction fidelity. We then, introduce a non-linear diffusion model that smoothly transitions latent representations corresponding to different </span><math id="abstract1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="abstract1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> values. This model denoises towards less disentangled and more informative representations, ultimately leading to (almost) lossless representations, enabling sharp reconstructions. Furthermore, our model supports sample generation without input images, functioning as a standalone generative model. We evaluate our framework in terms of both disentanglement and generation quality. Additionally, we observe smooth transitions in the latent spaces with respect to changes in </span><math id="abstract1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="abstract1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, facilitating consistent manipulation of generated outputs.</span></p>
  
</div>
<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1 </span>Introduction</h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Today, numerous advanced latent generative models are capable of producing hyperrealistic images, providing end users with a broad array of options. Current advancements in state-of-the-art generative models focus primarily on qualitative improvements in generated outputs, with recent research emphasizing the study and analysis of training dynamics to enhance generation quality <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bibx21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Karras et al., 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bibx22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Karras et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bibx18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hoogeboom et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bibx19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hoogeboom et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. Consequently, progress in generative modeling has largely shifted focus from learning and evaluating a model’s latent representations to refining the generation process itself. However, research on deep latent generative models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bibx27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kingma &amp; Welling, 2013</a>; <a href="#bib.bibx36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Radford et al., 2015</a>)</cite> and unsupervised representation learning has shown that purposefully learned representations not only enhance generative performance but also offer practical advantages  such as attribute and object changes <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bibx48" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al., 2023</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Previous generative modeling approaches aimed at learning disentangled and interpretable latent representations have often trailed behind in generation quality. <math id="S1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-VAE is a fundamental method for learning such representations, based on the variational autoencoder (VAE) framework <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bibx27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kingma &amp; Welling, 2013</a>)</cite>. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bibx15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Higgins et al. (2016)</a></cite> modified the VAE objective by introducing a hyperparameter <math id="S1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, where setting <math id="S1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1</annotation></semantics></math> recovers the original objective function. This <math id="S1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> parameter governs the degree of disentanglement, balancing it against reconstruction and generation quality. A larger <math id="S1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> value imposes stronger regularization on the latent space, empirically shown to promote disentanglement, while a smaller <math id="S1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> prioritizes reconstruction accuracy but does not encourage disentanglement. Although <math id="S1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-VAE has been extensively studied <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bibx26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim &amp; Mnih, 2018</a>; <a href="#bib.bibx3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2018</a>; <a href="#bib.bibx43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shao et al., 2020</a>; <a href="#bib.bibx6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dewangan &amp; Maurya, 2022</a>)</cite>, overcoming this challenging trade-off in general models remains difficult and has only been addressed by a few works <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bibx38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ren et al., 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bibx49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bibx46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2023</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Inspired by <math id="S1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-VAEs, we aim to promote disentangled representation learning within modern generative models. To this end, we propose a novel generative modeling framework. Our model consists of two main components, trained in a two-stage manner. First, we train a <em id="S1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">single</em> VAE that learns a spectrum of latent representations by varying the parameter <math id="S1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, which controls disentanglement through regularization. This VAE comprises an encoder and a decoder, each conditioned on <math id="S1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>. However, this VAE still faces the trade-off issue: disentangled latent representations with larger <math id="S1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> lose information about the original input, leading to blurred reconstructions similar to those of a standard <math id="S1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-VAE. To address this, we introduce a novel non-linear diffusion model that denoises the latent variable at a given <math id="S1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> back to an (ideally) non-lossy latent space corresponding to <math id="S1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0</annotation></semantics></math>. This allows us to generate sharp, non-blurred images by decoding the denoised latent variable (see <a href="#S2.F1" title="In 2 Overview of 𝛽-VAE ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In our experiments, we evaluate our model in terms of both disentanglement and generation quality. For disentanglement, we demonstrate that our model effectively achieves this purpose while maintaining generation performance, by following a well-established benchmark using CelebA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bibx49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2023</a>)</cite>. Additionally, we benchmark our approach on well-known toy datasets
 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bibx31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Locatello et al., 2019</a>; <a href="#bib.bibx24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Khrulkov et al., 2021</a>)</cite>. Furthermore, we test our model’s capability as a standalone generative model on widely-used image datasets both qualitatively and quantitatively.
We also show that the set of learned latent spaces is smooth with respect to <math id="S1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, which is essential for consistent manipulation.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Our contributions are briefly listed as follows.</p>
<ul id="S1.I1" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:20pt;">
<li id="S1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We propose a generative modeling framework that leverages multiple levels of latent representations, ranging from fully-informed to fully-disentangled, by extending <math id="S1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-VAE with a range of <math id="S1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> values, along with a novel model design and objective function.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We propose a novel non-linear diffusion model that connects latent spaces corresponding to different <math id="S1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> values. By combining the VAE and the diffusion model, our approach enables both disentanglement and high-quality generation in principle.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We empirically demonstrate that our model effectively balances disentanglement and image quality, achieving a superior trade-off compared to existing methods with the same motivation. Our approach attains disentanglement performance on par with disentanglement-focused baselines while generating high-quality images comparable to state-of-the-art generative models.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Overview of <math id="S2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-VAE</h2>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We begin with the formulation of a vanilla VAE </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bibx27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kingma &amp; Welling, 2013</a><span id="S2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Suppose we have a dataset </span><math id="S2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}=\{\bm{x}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}=\{\bm{x}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, where </span><math id="S2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℝ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> for </span><math id="S2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=\{1,\ldots,M\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=\{1,\ldots,M\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.We denote the empirical distribution defined by </span><math id="S2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> as </span><math id="S2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{D}}(\bm{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{D}}(\bm{x})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. A VAE aims to uncover a reduced set of latent factors that give rise to this dataset.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Specifically, a latent variable </span><math id="S2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℝ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (</span><math id="S2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d&lt;D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d&lt;D</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) is introduced, with its prior distribution set as </span><math id="S2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\bm{z})=\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\bm{I}_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝟎</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝑰</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\bm{z})=\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\bm{I}_{d})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Data samples are generated by first sampling </span><math id="S2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}\sim p(\bm{z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∼</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}\sim p(\bm{z})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and then decoding it using a probabilistic decoder, denoted as </span><math id="S2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}(\bm{x}|\bm{z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(\bm{x}|\bm{z})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. The decoder is commonly parameterized by a conditional isotropic Gaussian as </span><math id="S2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}(\bm{x}|\bm{z})=\mathcal{N}(\bm{x}|g_{\theta}(\bm{z}),s^{2}\bm{I}_{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">g</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝑰</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(\bm{x}|\bm{z})=\mathcal{N}(\bm{x}|g_{\theta}(\bm{z}),s^{2}\bm{I}_{D})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> with a non-negative scalar </span><math id="S2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p2.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and a function </span><math id="S2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\theta}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">g</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.278em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℝ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℝ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\theta}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p2.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.
We then wish to maximize the marginal log-likelihood </span><math id="S2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{p_{\mathcal{D}}(x)}\left[\log p_{\theta}(\bm{x})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{p_{\mathcal{D}}(x)}\left[\log p_{\theta}(\bm{x})\right]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p2.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, where </span><math id="S2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}(\bm{x})=\mathbb{E}_{p(\bm{z})}[p_{\theta}(\bm{x}|\bm{z})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(\bm{x})=\mathbb{E}_{p(\bm{z})}[p_{\theta}(\bm{x}|\bm{z})]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p2.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. However, this maximization is not tractable. Therefore, in the VAE framework, a surrogate objective function called the evidence lower bound (ELBO) is maximized instead, formulated as</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\log p_{\theta}(\bm{x})\geq\mathbb{E}_{q_{\phi}(\bm{z}|\bm{x})}\left[\log p_{\theta}(\bm{x}|\bm{z})\right]-\KL(q_{\phi}(\bm{z}|\bm{x})||p(\bm{z}))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">[</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">]</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D_{KL}</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log p_{\theta}(\bm{x})\geq\mathbb{E}_{q_{\phi}(\bm{z}|\bm{x})}\left[\log p_{\theta}(\bm{x}|\bm{z})\right]-\KL(q_{\phi}(\bm{z}|\bm{x})||p(\bm{z})),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where </span><math id="S2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\phi}(\bm{z}|\bm{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\phi}(\bm{z}|\bm{x})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p2.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is a variational distribution used to approximate the posterior distribution </span><math id="S2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}(\bm{z}|\bm{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(\bm{z}|\bm{x})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p2.2.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, a.k.a., the encoder. A common way to model this distribution is using a conditional Gaussian as </span><math id="S2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\phi}(\bm{z}|\bm{x})=\mathcal{N}(\bm{z}|\bm{f}_{\phi}(\bm{x}),\mathrm{diag}(\bm{\sigma}_{\phi}(\bm{x})))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒇</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝝈</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\phi}(\bm{z}|\bm{x})=\mathcal{N}(\bm{z}|\bm{f}_{\phi}(\bm{x}),\mathrm{diag}(\bm{\sigma}_{\phi}(\bm{x})))</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p2.2.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, with functions </span><math id="S2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{f}_{\phi}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}\mathbb{R}^{D}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒇</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.278em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℝ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℝ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{f}_{\phi}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}\mathbb{R}^{D}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p2.2.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><math id="S2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\sigma}_{\phi}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}\mathbb{R}^{D}\to\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝝈</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.278em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℝ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\sigma}_{\phi}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}\mathbb{R}^{D}\to\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p2.2.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Through the maximization of Eq. (</span><a href="#S2.E1" title="Equation 1 ‣ 2 Overview of 𝛽-VAE ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a><span id="S2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">), the encoder learns to recover latent generative factors from the dataset, while the decoder attempts to reconstruct </span><math id="S2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> from </span><math id="S2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> as accurately as possible. In other words, the encoder and decoder are trained to compress the data without information loss, effectively becoming stochastic inverses of each other. The </span><math id="S2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">-VAE </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S2.p3.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bibx15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Higgins et al., 2016</a><span id="S2.p3.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S2.p3.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is a variant of the above model that employs the following modified objective function: </span><math id="S2.p3.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{q_{\phi}(\bm{z}|\bm{x})}\left[\log p_{\theta}(\bm{x}|\bm{z})\right]-\beta\KL(q_{\phi}(\bm{z}|\bm{x})||p(\bm{z}))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">[</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">]</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D_{KL}</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{q_{\phi}(\bm{z}|\bm{x})}\left[\log p_{\theta}(\bm{x}|\bm{z})\right]-\beta\KL(q_{\phi}(\bm{z}|\bm{x})||p(\bm{z})),</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p3.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
where the </span><em id="S2.p3.1.11" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">regularization term</em><span id="S2.p3.1.12" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> in </span><a href="#S2.E1" title="In 2 Overview of 𝛽-VAE ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a><span id="S2.p3.1.13" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is scaled by a hyperparameter </span><math id="S2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p3.1.14" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The choice of </span><math id="S2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> creates a trade-off between the reconstruction quality and disentanglement of the latent representation. Previous works have established that increasing the contribution of the </span><em id="S2.p4.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">regularization term</em><span id="S2.p4.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, i.e., setting </span><math id="S2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p4.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, not only promotes independence among latent dimensions but also facilitates the learning of interpretable generative factors (please refer to Appendix </span><a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Supplementary for 𝛽-VAE ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a><span id="S2.p4.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> for this literature review). On the other hand, a downside to increasing regularization is the loss of information. When the variational approximation approaches the prior according to the KL term, all encodings </span><math id="S2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\phi}(\bm{z}|\bm{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\phi}(\bm{z}|\bm{x})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p4.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> begin to collapse to the prior, resulting in a lack of distinct information about individual data points, which hampers accurate reconstruction. This indicates that setting the value of </span><math id="S2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p4.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is non-trivial due to the precarious balance between desirable disentanglement and undesirable loss of information. Even with a suitable parameter </span><math id="S2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p4.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> for disentangled representation, reconstructed samples may still be blurred due to the loss of information.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2507.06613v1/main_figure.png" id="S2.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/240;" width="476" height="240" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S2.F1.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 1</span>: </span><span id="S2.F1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Our framework for achieving both disentanglement and generation.<span id="S2.F1.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Our approach embeds <math id="S2.F1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> values as time conditioning in our newly designed nonlinear diffusion model enabling both effective disentanglement and high-quality generation. (a-b) Directly decoding <math id="S2.F1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{b}</annotation></semantics></math> at non-zero <math id="S2.F1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> results in blurred images; however, applying the denoiser before decoding yields clear images. (c-d) The denoiser also improves the quality of manipulated images. By using the same direction in the latent space for these manipulations, we achieve consistent changes in age across different ground truth images. This demonstrates that our model produces a disentangled and easily controllable latent space. <span id="S2.F1.11.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">More examples of attribute changes can be found in <a href="#A4.F8" title="In D.5 Exploring the Spectrum of Learned Latents ‣ Appendix D Additional Results ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>.</span></span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">In the following sections, we propose our solutions to two critical issues:</span></p>
<ol id="S2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:20pt;">
<li id="S2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Problem 1:</span><span id="S2.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Choosing the optimal regularization coefficient (</span><math id="S2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) is nontrivial and requires multiple training runs. Our solution to this issue is detailed in </span><a href="#S3" title="3 Multi-𝛽 Representation Learning ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a><span id="S2.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Problem 2:</span><span id="S2.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="S2.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text">Achieving both generation quality and controllability is challenging, as the regularization used for learning disentangled representations often degrades reconstruction and sample quality. Our solution to this issue is detailed in <a href="#S4" title="4 Reversing the Information Loss ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Multi-<math id="S3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> Representation Learning</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To overcome the severe trade-off between reconstruction accuracy and the disentanglement of latent representation in existing VAE variants, we propose multi-</span><math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> latent representation learning. First, we extend </span><math id="S3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">-VAE by treating </span><math id="S3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> as a variable rather than a hyperparameter in Section </span><a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Conditional Multi-level 𝛽-VAE ‣ 3 Multi-𝛽 Representation Learning ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a><span id="S3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Using a monotonic property of multi-</span><math id="S3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> latent space presented in Section </span><a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Controlling Information Loss with 𝛽 ‣ 3 Multi-𝛽 Representation Learning ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a><span id="S3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, a subsequently learned diffusion model allows us to move across latent spaces corresponding to different </span><math id="S3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (see Section </span><a href="#S4" title="4 Reversing the Information Loss ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a><span id="S3.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">).</span></p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>Conditional Multi-level <math id="S3.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-VAE</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Here we extend the </span><math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">-VAE to incorporate </span><math id="S3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> as a variable within a range of values. In our setup, unlike the typical </span><math id="S3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">-VAE, </span><math id="S3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> lies in </span><math id="S3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,B]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,B]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> instead of being fixed, and it scales the reconstruction and regularization terms with weights of </span><math id="S3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(B-\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(B-\beta)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><math id="S3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, respectively (see </span><a href="#S3.E4" title="In 3.1 Conditional Multi-level 𝛽-VAE ‣ 3 Multi-𝛽 Representation Learning ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">). This approach allows us to achieve </span><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text"> a full spectrum of the weighting, encompassing both the reconstruction-only and regularization-only objectives as extreme cases with <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.</span><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
We expect that larger values of </span><math id="S3.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> result in more disentangled latent representations, while smaller values will yield higher fidelity in the reconstructed samples. We assume that each value of </span><math id="S3.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> has its latent space, which is denoted as </span><math id="S3.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Z</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.14" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.
In our VAE, the decoder and encoder for a given </span><math id="S3.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.15" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> are designed as follows:</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\theta}(\bm{x}|\bm{z}_{\beta};\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">;</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\theta}(\bm{x}|\bm{z}_{\beta};\beta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{N}(\bm{x}|\bm{g}_{\theta}(\bm{z}_{\beta},\beta),s^{2}_{\beta}\bm{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒈</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝑰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{N}(\bm{x}|\bm{g}_{\theta}(\bm{z}_{\beta},\beta),s^{2}_{\beta}\bm{I})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q_{\phi}(\bm{z}_{\beta}|\bm{x};\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">;</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q_{\phi}(\bm{z}_{\beta}|\bm{x};\beta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{N}(\bm{z}_{\beta}|\bm{f}_{\phi}(\bm{x},\beta),\sigma^{2}_{\beta}\bm{I})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒇</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝑰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{N}(\bm{z}_{\beta}|\bm{f}_{\phi}(\bm{x},\beta),\sigma^{2}_{\beta}\bm{I}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where </span><math id="S3.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{2}_{\beta}\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0},~\sigma^{2}_{\beta}\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{2}_{\beta}\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0},~\sigma^{2}_{\beta}\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, </span><math id="S3.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><math id="S3.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> represent the parameters for the decoder and encoder, respectively. Both the encoder and the decoder depend on </span><math id="S3.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p1.2.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, which induces different latent spaces. Additionally, the conditional covariance matrices in both the data and latent spaces are modeled as learnable isotropic matrices that depend solely on </span><math id="S3.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p1.2.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Under this model setup, we propose a novel objective function based on a rescaled ELBO as </span><math id="S3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}=\mathbb{E}_{\beta}\mathcal{L}_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}=\mathbb{E}_{\beta}\mathcal{L}_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, where</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{p_{\mathcal{D}}(\bm{x})}\Bigl[(B-\beta)\mathbb{E}_{q_{\phi}(\bm{z}_{\beta}|\bm{x})}\left[\log p_{\theta}(\bm{x}|\bm{z}_{\beta})\right]-\beta\KL(q_{\phi}(\bm{z}_{\beta}|\bm{x})||p(\bm{z}))\Bigr]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">[</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">]</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D_{KL}</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{p_{\mathcal{D}}(\bm{x})}\Bigl[(B-\beta)\mathbb{E}_{q_{\phi}(\bm{z}_{\beta}|\bm{x})}\left[\log p_{\theta}(\bm{x}|\bm{z}_{\beta})\right]-\beta\KL(q_{\phi}(\bm{z}_{\beta}|\bm{x})||p(\bm{z}))\Bigr],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">and we sample </span><math id="S3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p2.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> from a prior distribution to train the VAE across multiple </span><math id="S3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p2.2.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> values.
Notably, </span><math id="S3.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p2.2.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> when </span><math id="S3.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p2.2.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, with </span><math id="S3.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p2.2.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><math id="S3.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p2.2.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, corresponds to the objective functions for a plain autoencoder and a VAE, respectively, without considering the scaling factors</span><span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
              
              
              
              
              
              
              
            <span id="footnote1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Our <math id="footnote1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> is different from that of the typical <math id="footnote1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-VAE in the relationship between <math id="footnote1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> values and their respective models.</span></span></span></span><span id="S3.SS1.p2.2.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. </span><a href="#algorithm1" title="In 4.2 Non-linear Diffusion in Latent Space ‣ 4 Reversing the Information Loss ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a><span id="S3.SS1.p2.2.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> contains the training algorithm for this </span><span id="S3.SS1.p2.2.10" class="ltx_text">augmented</span><span id="S3.SS1.p2.2.11" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><math id="S3.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p2.2.12" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">-VAE.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Controlling Information Loss with <math id="S3.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">As outlined in the previous section, our objective function (</span><a href="#S3.E4" title="Equation 4 ‣ 3.1 Conditional Multi-level 𝛽-VAE ‣ 3 Multi-𝛽 Representation Learning ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a><span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) facilitates a smooth interpolation and extrapolation between the objectives of an autoencoder and a VAE. Specifically, the parameter </span><math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> modulates the degree of information retention in the latent spaces. To elucidate this mechanism, we present a simplified analysis of our novel objective function (</span><a href="#S3.E4" title="Equation 4 ‣ 3.1 Conditional Multi-level 𝛽-VAE ‣ 3 Multi-𝛽 Representation Learning ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a><span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) in the case of </span><math id="S3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. We anticipate that setting </span><math id="S3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;0.5</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> encourages disentanglement within the latent space </span><math id="S3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒵</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, albeit at the cost of information essential for accurate reconstruction. Conversely, choosing </span><math id="S3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&lt;0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&lt;0.5</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> enhances reconstruction fidelity but compromises the disentanglement of representations.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">A smaller </span><math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> value places greater emphasis on the reconstruction term, resulting in a reduced latent variance </span><math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\beta}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\beta}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.
In the extreme case, setting </span><math id="S3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> theoretically results in perfect reconstruction with </span><math id="S3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{0}^{2}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{0}^{2}=0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, as demonstrated in the following proposition. We defer the proofs to Appendix </span><a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Proofs ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a><span id="S3.SS2.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 3.1</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Under certain regularity conditions, the global optimum of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is achieved when <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{0}^{2}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{0}^{2}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">In contrast, increasing </span><math id="S3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> towards 1 enhances regularization, which encourages disentanglement of the latent representation. In the extreme case, when </span><math id="S3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, the objective function (</span><a href="#S3.E4" title="Equation 4 ‣ 3.1 Conditional Multi-level 𝛽-VAE ‣ 3 Multi-𝛽 Representation Learning ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a><span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) reduces to the KL regularization term, causing </span><math id="S3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\phi}(\bm{z}|\bm{x};\beta=1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">;</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\phi}(\bm{z}|\bm{x};\beta=1)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> collapse to the prior distribution </span><math id="S3.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\bm{z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\bm{z})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Consequently, the latent space, i.e., </span><math id="S3.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒵</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, no longer retains any information about the input </span><math id="S3.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, as demonstrated in the following proposition.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 3.2</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The mutual information between the input and the reconstructed samples produced by the VAE becomes zero as <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\KL(q_{\phi}(\bm{z}|\bm{x};\beta=1)\parallel p(\bm{z}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D_{KL}</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐳</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐱</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">;</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐳</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(q_{\phi}(\bm{z}|\bm{x};\beta=1)\parallel p(\bm{z}))</annotation></semantics></math> converges to zero. It holds for any decoder function <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="g_{\theta}(\cdot,\beta=1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">g</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\theta}(\cdot,\beta=1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The gradual loss of information in the latent space with </span><math id="S3.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is also characterised by a gradual increase in the variance of latent representations such that </span><math id="S3.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\beta}&lt;\sigma_{\beta^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\beta}&lt;\sigma_{\beta^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> for </span><math id="S3.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq\beta&lt;\beta^{\prime}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq\beta&lt;\beta^{\prime}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p4.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, which is also observed in previous studies </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S3.SS2.p4.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bibx44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Takida et al., 2022</a><span id="S3.SS2.p4.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S3.SS2.p4.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">In summary, our multi-level </span><math id="S3.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">-VAE is equipped to learn a slew of latent representations which due to </span><a href="#S3.E4" title="In 3.1 Conditional Multi-level 𝛽-VAE ‣ 3 Multi-𝛽 Representation Learning ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a><span id="S3.SS2.p5.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, capture major axes of variation present across the dataset by down-weighting accurate reconstructions. This does not mitigate Problem </span><a href="#S2.I1.i2" title="Item 2 ‣ 2 Overview of 𝛽-VAE ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a><span id="S3.SS2.p5.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.
To this end, we purposely combine the model </span><a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3.1 Conditional Multi-level 𝛽-VAE ‣ 3 Multi-𝛽 Representation Learning ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a><span id="S3.SS2.p5.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><a href="#S3.E4" title="In 3.1 Conditional Multi-level 𝛽-VAE ‣ 3 Multi-𝛽 Representation Learning ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a><span id="S3.SS2.p5.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> so that learnt </span><math id="S3.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p5.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> parallel a typical noising process in diffusion models (</span><math id="S3.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\equiv t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≡</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\equiv t</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p5.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">). When trained well, diffusion models can capture the target distribution and sample realisitic data by repeated denoising.
However, due to the involvement of an encoder that specifies the mean </span><math id="S3.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{f}_{\phi}(\bm{x},\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒇</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{f}_{\phi}(\bm{x},\beta)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p5.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> at all </span><math id="S3.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p5.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> in the latent space, our noising process diverges from the commonly used linear inference/noising process. We detail our formulation of non-linear denoising diffusion in the next section.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Reversing the Information Loss</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Increasing regularization enhances representation learning but negatively affects sample and reconstruction quality. At higher </span><math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> values, the reconstructions tend to collapse into an “averaged” image, a phenomenon also noted by </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bibx4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Collins et al. (2022)</a></cite><span id="S4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. To address Problem 2, we propose reversing information loss by training a denoising model based on a diffusion process. First, we review the standard diffusion model in </span><a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Primer on Diffusion Models ‣ 4 Reversing the Information Loss ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a><span id="S4.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and its nonlinear extension in </span><a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Non-linear Diffusion in Latent Space ‣ 4 Reversing the Information Loss ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a><span id="S4.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. In this approach, the time-varying mean is governed by the encoder (</span><math id="S4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{f}_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒇</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{f}_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">), with noise conditioning parameterized by </span><math id="S4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> or equivalently by time </span><math id="S4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Primer on Diffusion Models</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We start with a brief primer on the vanilla diffusion models with a linear diffusion process.
Diffusion models consist of a fixed hierarchical encoding process, known as the forward or noising process, and a decoding process for generation. In the encoding stage, incremental noise is gradually added to the data, transforming it into a Gaussian noise:</span></p>
<table id="S4.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\bm{z}_{t}|\bm{x};t)\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=\mathcal{N}(\bm{z}_{t}|\bm{x},\sigma^{2}_{t}\bm{I}_{d})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">;</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝑰</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\bm{z}_{t}|\bm{x};t)\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=\mathcal{N}(\bm{z}_{t}|\bm{x},\sigma^{2}_{t}\bm{I}_{d}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where </span><math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,T]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, </span><math id="S4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS1.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is a small constant, and </span><math id="S4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS1.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is a predefined noise schedule that increases with </span><math id="S4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS1.p1.2.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Next, the Markovian forward distributions are derived as</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q(\bm{z}_{t}|\bm{z}_{t-\tau})=\mathcal{N}(\bm{z}_{t}|\bm{z}_{t-\tau},\sigma^{2}_{t|t-\tau}\bm{I}_{d})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝑰</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q(\bm{z}_{t}|\bm{z}_{t-\tau})=\mathcal{N}(\bm{z}_{t}|\bm{z}_{t-\tau},\sigma^{2}_{t|t-\tau}\bm{I}_{d}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where </span><math id="S4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}_{t|t-\tau}=\sigma^{2}_{t}-\sigma^{2}_{t-\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}_{t|t-\tau}=\sigma^{2}_{t}-\sigma^{2}_{t-\tau}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS1.p1.3.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.
A tractable reverse decoding process is obtained via Bayes’ rule as</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q(\bm{z}_{t-\tau}|\bm{z}_{t},\bm{x})=\mathcal{N}(\bm{z}_{t-\tau}|{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{{\tilde{\bm{\mu}}_{t}(\bm{z}_{t},\bm{x})}}},{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{{\tilde{\sigma}_{t}^{2}}}}\bm{I}_{d})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝝁</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝑰</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q(\bm{z}_{t-\tau}|\bm{z}_{t},\bm{x})=\mathcal{N}(\bm{z}_{t-\tau}|{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{{\tilde{\bm{\mu}}_{t}(\bm{z}_{t},\bm{x})}}},{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{{\tilde{\sigma}_{t}^{2}}}}\bm{I}_{d}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{where }{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{{\tilde{\sigma}_{t}^{2}}}}=\frac{\sigma^{2}_{t|t-\tau}\sigma^{2}_{t-\tau}}{\sigma^{2}_{t}}\text{ and }\,\,\,{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{{\tilde{\bm{\mu}}_{t}(\bm{z}_{t},\bm{x})}}}=\frac{\sigma^{2}_{t-\tau}}{\sigma^{2}_{t}}\bm{z}_{t}+\frac{\sigma^{2}_{t|t-\tau}}{\sigma^{2}_{t}}\bm{x}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">where </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"> and </mtext><mo lspace="0.510em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝝁</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{where }{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{{\tilde{\sigma}_{t}^{2}}}}=\frac{\sigma^{2}_{t|t-\tau}\sigma^{2}_{t-\tau}}{\sigma^{2}_{t}}\text{ and }\,\,\,{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{{\tilde{\bm{\mu}}_{t}(\bm{z}_{t},\bm{x})}}}=\frac{\sigma^{2}_{t-\tau}}{\sigma^{2}_{t}}\bm{z}_{t}+\frac{\sigma^{2}_{t|t-\tau}}{\sigma^{2}_{t}}\bm{x}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Diffusion models are trained to match the generative reverse conditional distributions in </span><a href="#S4.E7" title="In 4.1 Primer on Diffusion Models ‣ 4 Reversing the Information Loss ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a><span id="S4.SS1.p1.4.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, and are generally parameterized as</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t-\tau}|\bm{z}_{t})\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=\mathcal{N}(\bm{z}_{t-\tau}|{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{{\bm{\mu}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t)}}},\sigma^{2}_{r}(t)\bm{I}_{d})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝝁</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝑰</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t-\tau}|\bm{z}_{t})\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=\mathcal{N}(\bm{z}_{t-\tau}|{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{{\bm{\mu}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t)}}},\sigma^{2}_{r}(t)\bm{I}_{d}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{where }{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{{\bm{\mu}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t)}}}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=\frac{\sigma^{2}_{t-\tau}}{\sigma^{2}_{t}}\bm{z}_{t}+\frac{\sigma^{2}_{t|t-\tau}}{\sigma^{2}_{t}}\hat{\bm{x}}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">where </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝝁</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{where }{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{{\bm{\mu}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t)}}}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=\frac{\sigma^{2}_{t-\tau}}{\sigma^{2}_{t}}\bm{z}_{t}+\frac{\sigma^{2}_{t|t-\tau}}{\sigma^{2}_{t}}\hat{\bm{x}}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{x}}_{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{x}}_{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS1.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is known as the </span><em id="S4.SS1.p1.5.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">denoiser</em><span id="S4.SS1.p1.5.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Equivalently, we parametrize it as a noise prediction model </span><math id="S4.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{\epsilon}}_{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{\epsilon}}_{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS1.p1.5.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, where
</span><math id="S4.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{x}}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t)=\bm{z}_{t}-\sigma_{t}\hat{\bm{\epsilon}}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{x}}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t)=\bm{z}_{t}-\sigma_{t}\hat{\bm{\epsilon}}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS1.p1.5.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. The loss function of a diffusion model is derived using an ELBO (by extending </span><a href="#S2.E1" title="In 2 Overview of 𝛽-VAE ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a><span id="S4.SS1.p1.5.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> with time hierarchy), aiming to match the conditional distributions in </span><a href="#S4.E7" title="In 4.1 Primer on Diffusion Models ‣ 4 Reversing the Information Loss ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a><span id="S4.SS1.p1.5.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><a href="#S4.E9" title="In 4.1 Primer on Diffusion Models ‣ 4 Reversing the Information Loss ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a><span id="S4.SS1.p1.5.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> over all </span><math id="S4.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,T]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS1.p1.5.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> using the KL divergence. This loss boils down to a simple regression loss:</span></p>
<table id="S4.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{\psi}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{{\mathbb{E}_{t,\bm{x}}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{t}|\bm{x}}}}}\left[\frac{1}{2{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{{\tilde{\sigma}_{t}^{2}}}}}\|{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{{\bm{\mu}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t)}}}-{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{{\tilde{\bm{\mu}}_{t}(\bm{z}_{t},\bm{x})}}}\|^{2}_{2}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">min</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">[</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝝁</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝝁</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{\psi}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{{\mathbb{E}_{t,\bm{x}}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{t}|\bm{x}}}}}\left[\frac{1}{2{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{{\tilde{\sigma}_{t}^{2}}}}}\|{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{{\bm{\mu}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t)}}}-{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{{\tilde{\bm{\mu}}_{t}(\bm{z}_{t},\bm{x})}}}\|^{2}_{2}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">By discretizing the time such that </span><math id="S4.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{iT/N\}_{i=0}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{iT/N\}_{i=0}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS1.p1.6.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> for the iterative decoding, we obtain a hierarchical generator:</span></p>
<table id="S4.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\psi}(\bm{x})=\int_{\bm{z}}p(\bm{x}|\bm{z}_{0})p(\bm{z}_{B})\prod_{i=1}^{{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{{N}}}}p_{\psi}\left(\bm{z}_{{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{{\frac{(i-1)T}{N}}}}}\Big|\bm{z}_{{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{{\frac{iT}{N}}}}}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∫</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></mfrac></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="1.600em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></mfrac></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\psi}(\bm{x})=\int_{\bm{z}}p(\bm{x}|\bm{z}_{0})p(\bm{z}_{B})\prod_{i=1}^{{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{{N}}}}p_{\psi}\left(\bm{z}_{{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{{\frac{(i-1)T}{N}}}}}\Big|\bm{z}_{{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{{\frac{iT}{N}}}}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p1.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where </span><math id="S4.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\bm{z}_{T})=\mathcal{N}(\bm{z}_{T}|0,\bm{I}_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝑰</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\bm{z}_{T})=\mathcal{N}(\bm{z}_{T}|0,\bm{I}_{d})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS1.p1.7.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Non-linear Diffusion in Latent Space</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We propose a non-linear (in </span><math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) denoising diffusion for use in our model. In this subsection, time variables </span><math id="S4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (and </span><math id="S4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) are interchangeable with </span><math id="S4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (and </span><math id="S4.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">), as they represent the same concept. We hinted in </span><a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Controlling Information Loss with 𝛽 ‣ 3 Multi-𝛽 Representation Learning ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a><span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> that our non-linear diffusion process is prescribed by the </span><math id="S4.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- or time-dependent encoder. Formally, the distribution of </span><math id="S4.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> for given </span><math id="S4.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is</span></p>
<table id="S4.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\phi}(\bm{z}_{t}|\bm{x};t)=\mathcal{N}(\bm{z}_{t}|{\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\bm{f}_{\phi}(\bm{x},t)},\sigma^{2}_{t}\bm{I}_{d})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">;</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">𝒇</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝑰</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\phi}(\bm{z}_{t}|\bm{x};t)=\mathcal{N}(\bm{z}_{t}|{\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\bm{f}_{\phi}(\bm{x},t)},\sigma^{2}_{t}\bm{I}_{d}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This expression is just an adaptation of </span><a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3.1 Conditional Multi-level 𝛽-VAE ‣ 3 Multi-𝛽 Representation Learning ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a><span id="S4.SS2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> with </span><math id="S4.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=t</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS2.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, and is more general than </span><a href="#S4.E5" title="In 4.1 Primer on Diffusion Models ‣ 4 Reversing the Information Loss ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a><span id="S4.SS2.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. We propose the nonlinear Markovian encoding process as</span></p>
<table id="S4.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\phi}(\bm{z}_{t}|\bm{z}_{t-\tau},\bm{x})=\mathcal{N}(\bm{z}_{t}|\bm{z}_{t-\tau}+{\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\bm{f}_{\phi}(\bm{x},t)-\bm{f}_{\phi}(\bm{x},t-\tau)},\sigma^{2}_{t|t-\tau})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">𝒇</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">𝒇</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">τ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\phi}(\bm{z}_{t}|\bm{z}_{t-\tau},\bm{x})=\mathcal{N}(\bm{z}_{t}|\bm{z}_{t-\tau}+{\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\bm{f}_{\phi}(\bm{x},t)-\bm{f}_{\phi}(\bm{x},t-\tau)},\sigma^{2}_{t|t-\tau}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This form closely resembles </span><a href="#S4.E6" title="In 4.1 Primer on Diffusion Models ‣ 4 Reversing the Information Loss ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a><span id="S4.SS2.p1.3.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Following the development in </span><a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Primer on Diffusion Models ‣ 4 Reversing the Information Loss ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a><span id="S4.SS2.p1.3.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, we now define the reverse of </span><a href="#S4.E14" title="In 4.2 Non-linear Diffusion in Latent Space ‣ 4 Reversing the Information Loss ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a><span id="S4.SS2.p1.3.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> as:</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q_{\phi}(\bm{z}_{t-\tau}|\bm{z}_{t},\bm{x})=\mathcal{N}(\bm{z}_{t-\tau}|\tilde{\bm{\mu}}_{t}(\bm{z}_{t},\bm{x}),\tilde{\sigma}_{t}^{2}\bm{I}_{d})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝝁</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝑰</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q_{\phi}(\bm{z}_{t-\tau}|\bm{z}_{t},\bm{x})=\mathcal{N}(\bm{z}_{t-\tau}|\tilde{\bm{\mu}}_{t}(\bm{z}_{t},\bm{x}),\tilde{\sigma}_{t}^{2}\bm{I}_{d}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{where }\tilde{\bm{\mu}}_{t}(\bm{z}_{t},\bm{x})=\frac{\sigma^{2}_{t-\tau}}{\sigma^{2}_{t}}\bm{z}_{t}+\frac{\sigma^{2}_{t|t-\tau}}{\sigma^{2}_{t}}\bm{x}+{\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\bm{f}_{\phi}(\bm{x},t-\tau)-\bm{f}_{\phi}(\bm{x},t)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">where </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝝁</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">𝒇</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">τ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">𝒇</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{where }\tilde{\bm{\mu}}_{t}(\bm{z}_{t},\bm{x})=\frac{\sigma^{2}_{t-\tau}}{\sigma^{2}_{t}}\bm{z}_{t}+\frac{\sigma^{2}_{t|t-\tau}}{\sigma^{2}_{t}}\bm{x}+{\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\bm{f}_{\phi}(\bm{x},t-\tau)-\bm{f}_{\phi}(\bm{x},t)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">with </span><math id="S4.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\sigma}_{t}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\sigma}_{t}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS2.p1.4.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> remaining the same as </span><a href="#S4.E8" title="In 4.1 Primer on Diffusion Models ‣ 4 Reversing the Information Loss ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a><span id="S4.SS2.p1.4.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.
Due to the additional </span><math id="S4.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{f}_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒇</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{f}_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS2.p1.4.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> terms in this flavour of the diffusion model, </span><math id="S4.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mu}_{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝝁</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mu}_{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS2.p1.4.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> cannot follow the same parameterization as in </span><a href="#S4.E10" title="In 4.1 Primer on Diffusion Models ‣ 4 Reversing the Information Loss ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a><span id="S4.SS2.p1.4.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Instead we introduce a new approach to express the mean prediction in this case, as follows:</span></p>
<table id="S4.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{{\bm{\mu}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t)}}}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=\frac{\sigma^{2}_{t-\tau}}{\sigma^{2}_{t}}\bm{z}_{t}+\frac{\sigma^{2}_{t|t-\tau}}{\sigma^{2}_{t}}\hat{\bm{x}}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t)+{\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\hat{\bm{\Delta}}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝝁</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">𝚫</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{{\bm{\mu}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t)}}}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=\frac{\sigma^{2}_{t-\tau}}{\sigma^{2}_{t}}\bm{z}_{t}+\frac{\sigma^{2}_{t|t-\tau}}{\sigma^{2}_{t}}\hat{\bm{x}}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t)+{\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\hat{\bm{\Delta}}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#S4.E17" title="In 4.2 Non-linear Diffusion in Latent Space ‣ 4 Reversing the Information Loss ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a><span id="S4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> introduces an extra predictor </span><math id="S4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{\Delta}}_{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚫</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{\Delta}}_{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> for learning the evolution of encodings with time. In practice, we train noise prediction, reparameterizing </span><math id="S4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{x}}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{x}}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> with </span><math id="S4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{\epsilon}}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{\epsilon}}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS2.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, along with an encoding difference predictor </span><math id="S4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{\Delta}}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚫</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{\Delta}}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS2.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, which is novel to the best of our knowledge.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.SS2.fig1" class="ltx_figure">
<table id="S4.SS2.fig1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S4.SS2.fig1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.SS2.fig1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="S4.SS2.fig1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:162.2pt;">
<span id="algorithm1" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<span class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span>Training of our VAE</span>
<span id="algorithm1.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<span id="algorithm1.6.1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
<span id="algorithm1.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm1.6.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span>Dataset <math id="algorithm1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="algorithm1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-schedule <math id="algorithm1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\beta_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">{</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\beta_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, learning rate <math id="algorithm1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, number of training steps <math id="algorithm1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span>
<span id="algorithm1.6.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span id="algorithm1.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Trained networks, </span><math id="algorithm1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm1.6.2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, </span><math id="algorithm1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm1.6.2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, and </span><math id="algorithm1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\sigma}=\{\sigma_{\beta}\}_{\beta\in\{\beta_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝝈</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">β</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">β</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">N</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\sigma}=\{\sigma_{\beta}\}_{\beta\in\{\beta_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}}</annotation></semantics></math>
</span>
<span id="algorithm1.6.3" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">for</span><span id="algorithm1.6.3.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><em id="algorithm1.6.3.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><math id="algorithm1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=1,2,\dots,S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=1,2,\dots,S</annotation></semantics></math></em><span id="algorithm1.6.3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">do</span>
</span>
<span id="algorithm1.6.4" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.4.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span>
                          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1</span></span>
                        <span id="algorithm1.6.4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Sample: </span><math id="algorithm1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}\sim p_{\mathcal{D}}(\bm{x}),\ \beta\sim\mathcal{U}([0,1]),\ \bm{\epsilon}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\bm{I}_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝒟</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.627em">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">∼</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.627em">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">∼</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝟎</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝑰</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">d</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}\sim p_{\mathcal{D}}(\bm{x}),\ \beta\sim\mathcal{U}([0,1]),\ \bm{\epsilon}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\bm{I}_{d})</annotation></semantics></math>
</span>
<span id="algorithm1.6.5" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.5.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span>
                          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2</span></span>
                        <span id="algorithm1.6.5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Generate noisy encoding: </span><math id="algorithm1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}_{\beta}=\bm{f}_{\phi}(\bm{x},\beta)+\sigma_{\beta}\bm{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">β</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝒇</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}_{\beta}=\bm{f}_{\phi}(\bm{x},\beta)+\sigma_{\beta}\bm{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>
</span>
<span id="algorithm1.6.6" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.6.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span>
                          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">3</span></span>
                        <span id="algorithm1.6.6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Compute the objective </span><math id="algorithm1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm1.6.6.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> based on </span><a href="#S3.E4" title="In 3.1 Conditional Multi-level 𝛽-VAE ‣ 3 Multi-𝛽 Representation Learning ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>
</span>
<span id="algorithm1.6.7" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.7.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span>
                          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">4</span></span>
                        <span id="algorithm1.6.7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Update parameters: </span><math id="algorithm1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega\leftarrow\omega-\eta\nabla_{\omega}\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">ω</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">ω</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">ω</mi></msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega\leftarrow\omega-\eta\nabla_{\omega}\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm1.6.7.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, where </span><math id="algorithm1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega=\{\theta,\phi,\bm{\sigma}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">ω</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝝈</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega=\{\theta,\phi,\bm{\sigma}\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm1.6.7.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span>
</span>
<span id="algorithm1.6.8" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">return</span><span id="algorithm1.6.8.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><math id="algorithm1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{f}_{\phi},\bm{g}_{\theta},\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝒇</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝒈</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{f}_{\phi},\bm{g}_{\theta},\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>
</span>
<span id="algorithm1.6.9" class="ltx_listingline">
</span>
</span>
</span></span></td>
<td id="S4.SS2.fig1.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span id="S4.SS2.fig1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:162.2pt;">
<span id="algorithm2" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<span class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span>Sampling of our diffusion</span>
<span id="algorithm2.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<span id="algorithm2.6.1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span>
</span>
<span id="algorithm2.6.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.6.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span id="algorithm2.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span><span id="algorithm2.6.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Trained model </span><math id="algorithm2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\epsilon}_{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">ψ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\epsilon}_{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm2.6.2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, total time steps </span><math id="algorithm2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm2.6.2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, largest time </span><math id="algorithm2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm2.6.2.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, trained noise schedule </span><math id="algorithm2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\sigma}=\{\sigma_{t}\}_{t\in\{0,T/N,\ldots,(N-1)T/N,T\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝝈</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">N</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">T</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">N</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">T</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\sigma}=\{\sigma_{t}\}_{t\in\{0,T/N,\ldots,(N-1)T/N,T\}}</annotation></semantics></math>
</span>
<span id="algorithm2.6.3" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.6.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span id="algorithm2.6.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> </span><span id="algorithm2.6.3.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Generated sample </span><math id="algorithm2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝒛</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>
</span>
<span id="algorithm2.6.4" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.6.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Initialize:</span><span id="algorithm2.6.4.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><math id="algorithm2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}_{T}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\bm{I}_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">T</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">∼</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝟎</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝑰</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">d</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}_{T}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\bm{I}_{d})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm2.6.4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span><span id="algorithm2.6.4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">for</span><span id="algorithm2.6.4.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><em id="algorithm2.6.4.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><math id="algorithm2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=T,(N-1)T/N\ldots,T/N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=T,(N-1)T/N\ldots,T/N</annotation></semantics></math></em><span id="algorithm2.6.4.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="algorithm2.6.4.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">do</span>
</span>
<span id="algorithm2.6.5" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.6.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm2.6.5.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span>
                          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.6.5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1.</span></span>
                        <span id="algorithm2.6.5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Predict noise and diff: </span>
</span>
<span id="algorithm2.6.6" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.6.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm2.6.6.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><math id="algorithm2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{\epsilon}}=\hat{\bm{\epsilon}}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t),\;\hat{\bm{\Delta}}=\hat{\bm{\Delta}}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝚫</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝚫</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{\epsilon}}=\hat{\bm{\epsilon}}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t),\;\hat{\bm{\Delta}}=\hat{\bm{\Delta}}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t)</annotation></semantics></math>
</span>
<span id="algorithm2.6.7" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.6.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm2.6.7.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span>
                          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.6.7.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2.</span></span>
                        <span id="algorithm2.6.7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Compute mean for </span><math id="algorithm2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">z</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm2.6.7.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:</span>
</span>
<span id="algorithm2.6.8" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.6.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm2.6.8.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><math id="algorithm2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mu}_{t}=\bm{z}_{t}-\sigma_{t}\hat{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝝁</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">ϵ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mu}_{t}=\bm{z}_{t}-\sigma_{t}\hat{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm2.6.8.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span>
                          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.6.8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">3.</span></span>
                        <span id="algorithm2.6.8.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Predict previous mean: </span><math id="algorithm2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mu}_{t-T/N}=\bm{\mu}_{t}-\hat{\bm{\Delta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝝁</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">N</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝝁</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝚫</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mu}_{t-T/N}=\bm{\mu}_{t}-\hat{\bm{\Delta}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm2.6.8.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span>
                          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.6.8.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">4.</span></span>
                        <span id="algorithm2.6.8.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Update </span><math id="algorithm2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}_{t-T/N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝒛</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">N</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}_{t-T/N}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm2.6.8.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (with </span><math id="algorithm2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\varepsilon}\sim\mathcal{N}(\bm{0},\bm{I}_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝜺</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">∼</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝟎</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝑰</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">d</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\varepsilon}\sim\mathcal{N}(\bm{0},\bm{I}_{d})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm2.6.8.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">):</span><math id="algorithm2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}_{t-T/N}=\bm{\mu}_{t-T/N}+\sigma_{t-T/N}\bm{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝒛</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">N</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝝁</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">N</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">σ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">N</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝜺</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}_{t-T/N}=\bm{\mu}_{t-T/N}+\sigma_{t-T/N}\bm{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm2.6.8.11" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span>
</span>
<span id="algorithm2.6.9" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.6.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">return</span><span id="algorithm2.6.9.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><math id="algorithm2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">𝒛</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>
</span>
<span id="algorithm2.6.10" class="ltx_listingline">
</span>
</span>
</span></span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Following the parameterization of </span><math id="S4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mu}_{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝝁</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mu}_{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, our model training differs from standard practice in a couple of key ways. First, we do not train the noise prediction network to predict the noise added to </span><math id="S4.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}_{0}=f_{\phi}(\bm{x},0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}_{0}=f_{\phi}(\bm{x},0)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS2.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> given a sample </span><math id="S4.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS2.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. The transition from </span><math id="S4.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS2.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to </span><math id="S4.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS2.p3.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is non-linear due to the encoder and depends on its Jacobian, </span><math id="S4.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\dif\bm{f}_{\phi}(\bm{x},t)}{\dif t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mo lspace="0.047em">⁡</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐟</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐱</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mo lspace="0.047em">⁡</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\dif\bm{f}_{\phi}(\bm{x},t)}{\dif t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS2.p3.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Rather than learning an inversion of this time-varying encoding, we aim to learn the direction of the noise (</span><math id="S4.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\epsilon}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\epsilon}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS2.p3.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) at each time step </span><math id="S4.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,T]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS2.p3.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> using </span><math id="S4.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{\epsilon}}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{\epsilon}}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS2.p3.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{t,\bm{x}}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\epsilon}_{t}}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{t}|\bm{x},\bm{\epsilon}_{t}}\left[\frac{1}{w(t)}\|\hat{\bm{\epsilon}}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t)-\bm{\epsilon}_{t}\|^{2}_{2}\right]\text{ with }\bm{z}_{t}=\bm{f}_{\phi}(\bm{x},t)+\sigma_{t}\bm{\epsilon}_{t}\text{ and }\bm{\epsilon}_{t}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\bm{I}_{d})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"> with </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒇</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∼</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝟎</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝑰</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{t,\bm{x}}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\epsilon}_{t}}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{t}|\bm{x},\bm{\epsilon}_{t}}\left[\frac{1}{w(t)}\|\hat{\bm{\epsilon}}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t)-\bm{\epsilon}_{t}\|^{2}_{2}\right]\text{ with }\bm{z}_{t}=\bm{f}_{\phi}(\bm{x},t)+\sigma_{t}\bm{\epsilon}_{t}\text{ and }\bm{\epsilon}_{t}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\bm{I}_{d}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where </span><math id="S4.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(t)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS2.p3.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is a weighting function. This approach trains the model to denoise at each time step. Additionally, </span><math id="S4.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{\Delta}}_{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚫</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{\Delta}}_{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS2.p3.2.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is necessary for sampling and is trained to predict the change in </span><math id="S4.SS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{f}_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒇</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{f}_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS2.p3.2.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> over a small time interval </span><math id="S4.SS2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
              
              
              
              
              
              
              
            In implementation, we set <math id="footnote2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=T/N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=T/N</annotation></semantics></math> in the discrete time setup, learning the single time-step encoding difference for all times.</span></span></span><span id="S4.SS2.p3.2.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Assuming that the encoder is a smooth function,
this design is based on the intuition that learning encoding differences over one time step is easier than over arbitrarily large steps.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We adjust the diffusion model’s U-Net to produce two outputs, </span><math id="S4.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{\epsilon}}(\bm{z}_{t},t),\&gt;\hat{\bm{\Delta}}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.387em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚫</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{\epsilon}}(\bm{z}_{t},t),\&gt;\hat{\bm{\Delta}}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS2.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Using these predictions, we build our DDPM </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S4.SS2.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bibx16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ho et al., 2020</a><span id="S4.SS2.p4.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S4.SS2.p4.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">-inspired sampling algorithm, as shown in </span><a href="#algorithm2" title="In 4.2 Non-linear Diffusion in Latent Space ‣ 4 Reversing the Information Loss ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a><span id="S4.SS2.p4.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. The actual loss function used to train this new diffusion model is defined as</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{t,\bm{x}}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\epsilon}_{t}}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{t}|\bm{x},\bm{\epsilon}_{t}}\Bigl[\frac{1}{w(t)}\|\hat{\bm{\epsilon}}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t)-\bm{\epsilon}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{\epsilon}_{t})\|^{2}_{2}+{\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\|\bm{f}_{\phi}(\bm{x},t-\tau)-\bm{f}_{\phi}(\bm{x},t)-\hat{\bm{\Delta}}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t)\|_{2}^{2}}\Bigr]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">𝒇</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">τ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">𝒇</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">𝚫</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">2</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{t,\bm{x}}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\epsilon}_{t}}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{t}|\bm{x},\bm{\epsilon}_{t}}\Bigl[\frac{1}{w(t)}\|\hat{\bm{\epsilon}}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t)-\bm{\epsilon}_{t}(\bm{x},\bm{\epsilon}_{t})\|^{2}_{2}+{\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\|\bm{f}_{\phi}(\bm{x},t-\tau)-\bm{f}_{\phi}(\bm{x},t)-\hat{\bm{\Delta}}_{\psi}(\bm{z}_{t},t)\|_{2}^{2}}\Bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Integrating the conditional multilevel </span><math id="S4.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS2.p4.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">-VAE, as introduced in </span><a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Conditional Multi-level 𝛽-VAE ‣ 3 Multi-𝛽 Representation Learning ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a><span id="S4.SS2.p4.2.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, with the diffusion model described in </span><a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Non-linear Diffusion in Latent Space ‣ 4 Reversing the Information Loss ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a><span id="S4.SS2.p4.2.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is key to mitigating the disentanglement-reconstruction trade-off in our framework.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We now combine the two proposed modules from </span><a href="#S3" title="3 Multi-𝛽 Representation Learning ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a><span id="S4.SS2.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><a href="#S4" title="4 Reversing the Information Loss ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a><span id="S4.SS2.p5.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> into a single model, trained in two phases. In the first phase, we train the conditional multilevel </span><math id="S4.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS2.p5.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">-VAE using the loss defined in </span><a href="#S3.E4" title="In 3.1 Conditional Multi-level 𝛽-VAE ‣ 3 Multi-𝛽 Representation Learning ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a><span id="S4.SS2.p5.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (</span><a href="#algorithm1" title="In 4.2 Non-linear Diffusion in Latent Space ‣ 4 Reversing the Information Loss ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a><span id="S4.SS2.p5.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">). After this, we train the non-linear diffusion model from </span><a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Non-linear Diffusion in Latent Space ‣ 4 Reversing the Information Loss ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a><span id="S4.SS2.p5.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, keeping the autoencoder parameters fixed. Additionally, depending on the dataset, we fine-tune the decoder with an adversarial loss, following </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bibx40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rombach et al. (2021)</a></cite><span id="S4.SS2.p5.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, to enhance generation quality. Further training details are provided in </span><a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Details of experiments ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a><span id="S4.SS2.p5.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Related Works</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">-VAE and its variants have been extensively studied for their distinct capabilities </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bibx2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Burgess et al., 2017</a><span id="S5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S5.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and wide-ranging applications in domains such as images </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S5.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bibx15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Higgins et al., 2016</a><span id="S5.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S5.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, text </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S5.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bibx43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shao et al., 2020</a><span id="S5.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S5.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, and molecular generation </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S5.p1.1.14" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bibx39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Richards &amp; Groener, 2022</a><span id="S5.p1.1.16" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S5.p1.1.17" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. These models are especially valued for their interpretable latent representations, achieved through </span><math id="S5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.p1.1.18" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">-controlled regularization.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bibx26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim &amp; Mnih (2018)</a></cite><span id="S5.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> improved disentanglement while maintaining reconstruction quality by combining the ELBO with a total correlation term. Similarly, </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bibx3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al. (2018)</a></cite><span id="S5.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> enhanced mutual information between latent variables and observed data to promote independence among latent factors. </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bibx43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shao et al. (2020)</a></cite><span id="S5.p2.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> introduced an adaptive feedback mechanism that adjusts </span><math id="S5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.p2.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> during training based on KL divergence. </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bibx6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dewangan &amp; Maurya (2022)</a></cite><span id="S5.p2.1.13" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> applied a deep convolutional </span><math id="S5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.p2.1.14" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">-VAE for feature extraction in industrial fault diagnosis, using a variable </span><math id="S5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.p2.1.15" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> training protocol without conditioning the encoder and decoder on </span><math id="S5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.p2.1.16" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Both </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bibx4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Collins et al. (2022)</a></cite><span id="S5.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bibx1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bae et al. (2023)</a></cite><span id="S5.p3.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> investigated training VAEs with multiple </span><math id="S5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.p3.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> values, with </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bibx1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bae et al. (2023)</a></cite><span id="S5.p3.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> capturing the full rate-distortion curve using a hypernetwork conditioned on </span><math id="S5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.p3.1.12" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, and </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bibx4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Collins et al. (2022)</a></cite><span id="S5.p3.1.15" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> focusing on particle physics applications. In contrast, our framework enables high-fidelity generation from disentangled representations (with larger </span><math id="S5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.p3.1.16" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) by linking latent spaces through a novel non-linear diffusion process, along with specific adjustments to the </span><math id="S5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.p3.1.17" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">-conditioned VAE to optimize the latent space for diffusion.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Recently, a few methods have emerged to achieve disentanglement while preserving generation fidelity. </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bibx47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al. (2023a)</a></cite><span id="S5.p4.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> developed InfoDiffusion, a pioneering diffusion-based model that extends the Diffusion Autoencoder </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S5.p4.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(DiffAE, </span><a href="#bib.bibx35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Preechakul et al., 2022</a><span id="S5.p4.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S5.p4.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bibx49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al. (2023)</a></cite><span id="S5.p4.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> introduced DisDiff, which adds encoder and decoder components to pre-trained diffusion models to maintain generation quality, rather than training disentanglement-focused models from scratch. </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bibx38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ren et al. (2022)</a></cite><span id="S5.p4.1.14" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> focus on building an exploration technique for pre-trained generative models for post-hoc identification of disentangled directions. Notably, in contrast to training-free methods our approach encourages disentanglement during training, assuring a more disentangled representation.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Our method falls within the model-training-based category, similar to InfoDiffusion, but it uniquely learns a spectrum of latent representations that provide a distinct advantage. Combined with the learned non-linear diffusion model, our framework enables transitions between highly disentangled and fully informed latent representations, facilitating the generation of high-fidelity outputs.Additionally, we show in </span><a href="#A4.SS1" title="D.1 Orthogonality of our method and DisCo ‣ Appendix D Additional Results ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a><span id="S5.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (see </span><a href="#A4.T7" title="In D.1 Orthogonality of our method and DisCo ‣ Appendix D Additional Results ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a><span id="S5.p5.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) that finding-based methods like DisCo </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S5.p5.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bibx38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ren et al., 2022</a><span id="S5.p5.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S5.p5.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> can complement our approach, indicating potential for combined implementations.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Experiments</h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We quantitatively demonstrate that our method achieves both disentanglement and high-quality generation within a single model. We will focus on each of these aspects individually. Specifically, in </span><a href="#S6.SS1" title="6.1 Evaluating Disentanglement ‣ 6 Experiments ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a><span id="S6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, we examine the disentanglement of the learned latent representations. In </span><a href="#S6.SS2" title="6.2 Evaluating Generation Quality ‣ 6 Experiments ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.2</span></a><span id="S6.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, we evaluate our model’s unconditional generation performance and report standard metrics on commonly used image datasets. Additional details regarding the experiments can be found in the appendix.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.T1" class="ltx_table ltx_align_floatright" style="width:44%;">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>TAD and FID scores on CelebA. Our model outperforms baselines in terms both of disentanglement and generation quality.</figcaption>
