<section id="S6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.2 </span>Evaluating Generation Quality</h3>

<div id="S6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We demonstrate that our model can serve as a standalone generation model by evaluating its generation quality on practical image datasets, including CelebA-HQ </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S6.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bibx20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Karras et al., 2018</a><span id="S6.SS2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S6.SS2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, FFHQ </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S6.SS2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bibx23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Karras et al., 2019</a><span id="S6.SS2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S6.SS2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, and LSUN-Bedrooms </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S6.SS2.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bibx51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yu et al., 2015</a><span id="S6.SS2.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S6.SS2.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, at a resolution of </span><math id="S6.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="256\times 256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">256</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">256</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">256\times 256</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.SS2.p1.1.14" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. For these image datasets, we evaluate our model using FID to assess image quality and precision-recall </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S6.SS2.p1.1.15" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bibx28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kynkäänniemi et al., 2019</a><span id="S6.SS2.p1.1.17" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S6.SS2.p1.1.18" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to gauge data distribution coverage. Details of our architecture and training times are provided in </span><a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Details of experiments ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a><span id="S6.SS2.p1.1.19" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, and generated sample images are shown in </span><a href="#A4.SS4" title="D.4 Generated Samples from Noise ‣ Appendix D Additional Results ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.4</span></a><span id="S6.SS2.p1.1.20" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">While our model is designed to learn disentangled latent representations, it is crucial that this capability does not compromise generation quality. Based on our comparative performance with generation-focused baselines in </span><a href="#S6.T3" title="In 6.2 Evaluating Generation Quality ‣ 6 Experiments ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a><span id="S6.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, we conclude that our model effectively generates high-quality images at this resolution across various datasets.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Lastly, we visualize generated samples from various </span><math id="S6.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.SS2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> values in </span><a href="#S6.F2" title="In 6.2 Evaluating Generation Quality ‣ 6 Experiments ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a><span id="S6.SS2.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to demonstrate the smoothness of our latent space spectrum in terms of </span><math id="S6.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.SS2.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> or </span><math id="S6.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.SS2.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. We encode ground truth images to latent representations at certain </span><math id="S6.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.SS2.p3.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> values, denoise them using our non-linear diffusion, and decode them to obtain clear images. We observe that generated images with different values of </span><math id="S6.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.SS2.p3.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> remain consistent with each other. Another smoothness perspective, spatial smoothness of the latent spaces, is visualized in </span><a href="#A4.SS5" title="D.5 Exploring the Spectrum of Learned Latents ‣ Appendix D Additional Results ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.5</span></a><span id="S6.SS2.p3.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S6.T3.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:75%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="S6.T3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:75%;">Generation Quality.<span id="S6.T3.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
We evaluate our model for unconditional image synthesis and report standard metrics, comparing them against baselines specifically designed for generation.</span></span></figcaption>
<div id="S6.T3.8" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:25.5pt;vertical-align:-12.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-510.5pt,37.7pt) scale(0.252571899827865,0.252571899827865) ;">
<table id="S6.T3.8.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S6.T3.8.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T3.8.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:1.0pt;padding-right:1.0pt;" colspan="4"><span id="S6.T3.8.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">CelebA-HQ 256 <math id="S6.T3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> 256</span></th>
<th id="S6.T3.8.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:1.0pt;padding-right:1.0pt;" colspan="4"><span id="S6.T3.8.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">FFHQ 256 <math id="S6.T3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> 256</span></th>
<th id="S6.T3.8.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:1.0pt;padding-right:1.0pt;" colspan="4"><span id="S6.T3.8.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">LSUN-Bedrooms 256 <math id="S6.T3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> 256</span></th></tr>
<tr id="S6.T3.8.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T3.8.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:1.0pt;padding-right:1.0pt;"><span id="S6.T3.8.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Method</span></th>
<th id="S6.T3.8.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:1.0pt;padding-right:1.0pt;"><span id="S6.T3.8.1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">FID <math id="S6.T3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></th>
<th id="S6.T3.8.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:1.0pt;padding-right:1.0pt;"><span id="S6.T3.8.1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Prec. <math id="S6.T3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></th>
