<div id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The architecture of our multi-</span><math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> VAE and nonlinear diffusion model is designed to match that of </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bibx49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al. (2023)</a></cite><span id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, with details presented in </span><a href="#A3.T4" title="In C.1.1 Disentanglement on Face Images ‣ C.1 Details of Implementation ‣ Appendix C Details of experiments ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a><span id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><a href="#A3.T5" title="In C.1.1 Disentanglement on Face Images ‣ C.1 Details of Implementation ‣ Appendix C Details of experiments ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a><span id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, respectively. For evaluation, we use the Total AUROC Difference metric and the code provided by </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bibx50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yeats et al. (2022)</a></cite><span id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">C.1.2 </span>Disentanglement on Toy Experiments</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To ascertain the representations learned by our method in </span><a href="#S6.SS1" title="6.1 Evaluating Disentanglement ‣ 6 Experiments ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a><span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, we utilize small multi-</span><math id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> VAE architectures and employ the same convolutional backbone for implementing the baselines. Unlike previous works, we do not incorporate feed-forward layers in the architecture of the encoders and decoders. We assess the convergence of the model using the reconstruction loss.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For the architecture, all input images are resized to </span><math id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="64\times 64\times 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">64</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">64</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">64\times 64\times 3</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, and we do not apply any data augmentation when training the multi-</span><math id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> VAE. For all methods presented in </span><a href="#S6.T2" title="In 6.1.2 Common Benchmark with Toy Datasets ‣ 6.1 Evaluating Disentanglement ‣ 6 Experiments ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a><span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, we use a latent dimensionality of </span><math id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">32</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. The encoder and decoder are symmetric networks that are fully convolutional. The encoder consists of four layers with </span><math id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[64,64,128,256]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">64</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">64</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">128</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">256</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[64,64,128,256]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> channels, respectively, and we apply </span><span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">GroupNorm</span><span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> after every convolutional layer, followed by a </span><span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Sigmoid</span><span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> non-linearity.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For training these models, we select a batch size of </span><math id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="150" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">150</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">150</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and continue training until convergence is reached for each model. We used one NVIDIA L40S GPU for training on all these toy datasets. We trained our VAE with 500 values of </span><math id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> equally spaced within the range </span><math id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. We perform a sweep over all </span><math id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> values in our model to identify the optimal latent representation for each dataset. Specifically, for Cars3D, we achieve the highest score at </span><math id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=285/500" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">285</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">500</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=285/500</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">; for Shapes3D, at </span><math id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=210/500" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">210</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">500</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=210/500</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">; and for MPI3D, at </span><math id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=280/500" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">280</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">500</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=280/500</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. </span><a href="#S6.T2" title="In 6.1.2 Common Benchmark with Toy Datasets ‣ 6.1 Evaluating Disentanglement ‣ 6 Experiments ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a><span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> demonstrates that our model achieves disentanglement performance comparable to or surpassing that of other disentanglement models.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">C.1.3 </span>Unconditional Image Generation</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For architectures used in </span><a href="#S6.SS2" title="6.2 Evaluating Generation Quality ‣ 6 Experiments ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.2</span></a><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, we follow </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bibx40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rombach et al. (2021)</a></cite><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and use architectures present in their code base. For all data sets, we used an image resolution of </span><math id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="256\times 256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">256</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">256</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">256\times 256</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and compress the input by a factor of 8 leading to a latent dimensionality of </span><math id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32\times 32\times 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">32</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">32</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32\times 32\times 4</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. We fix the multi-</span><math id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> VAE architecture across datasets with the encoder and decoder each containing </span><math id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> layers, each comprising </span><math id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> ResNet </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bibx13" title="" class="ltx_ref">He et al., 2016</a><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.14" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> blocks with </span><math id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[128,\ 256,\ 512,\ 768]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">128</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"> 256</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"> 512</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"> 768</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[128,\ 256,\ 512,\ 768]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.15" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> channels, respectively.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm3" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_middle ltx_framed ltx_framed_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 3</span> </span>Forward Pass for ResNet Block with Time Embedding</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm3.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm3.6.1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.6.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span><span id="algorithm3.6.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span id="algorithm3.6.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span><span id="algorithm3.6.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Input </span><math id="algorithm3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm3.6.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, Temporal embedding </span><math id="algorithm3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="temb" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">temb</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.6.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.6.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span id="algorithm3.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> </span><span id="algorithm3.6.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Output </span><math id="algorithm3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.6.3" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.6.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><math id="algorithm3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\leftarrow x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">←</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\leftarrow x</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm3.6.3.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.6.4" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.6.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><math id="algorithm3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\leftarrow\texttt{GroupNorm}(h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">GroupNorm</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\leftarrow\texttt{GroupNorm}(h)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm3.6.4.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.6.5" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.6.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><math id="algorithm3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\leftarrow\texttt{Sigmoid}(h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">Sigmoid</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\leftarrow\texttt{Sigmoid}(h)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm3.6.5.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.6.6" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.6.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><math id="algorithm3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\leftarrow\texttt{Conv}(h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">Conv</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\leftarrow\texttt{Conv}(h)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm3.6.6.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.6.7" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.6.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><math id="algorithm3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\leftarrow h+\texttt{Proj}(\texttt{Sigmoid}(temb))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">Proj</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">Sigmoid</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\leftarrow h+\texttt{Proj}(\texttt{Sigmoid}(temb))</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.6.8" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.6.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><math id="algorithm3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\leftarrow\texttt{GroupNorm}(h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">GroupNorm</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\leftarrow\texttt{GroupNorm}(h)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm3.6.8.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.6.9" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.6.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><math id="algorithm3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\leftarrow\texttt{Sigmoid}(h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">Sigmoid</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\leftarrow\texttt{Sigmoid}(h)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm3.6.9.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.6.10" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.6.10.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><math id="algorithm3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\leftarrow\texttt{Dropout}(h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">Dropout</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\leftarrow\texttt{Dropout}(h)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm3.6.10.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.6.11" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.6.11.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><math id="algorithm3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\leftarrow\texttt{Conv}(h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">Conv</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\leftarrow\texttt{Conv}(h)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm3.6.11.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.6.12" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.6.12.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><span id="algorithm3.6.12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">return</span><span id="algorithm3.6.12.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><em id="algorithm3.6.12.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><math id="algorithm3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x+h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x+h</annotation></semantics></math></em><span id="algorithm3.6.12.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.6.13" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We present a simplified version of the ResNet block we use in </span><a href="#algorithm3" title="In C.1.3 Unconditional Image Generation ‣ C.1 Details of Implementation ‣ Appendix C Details of experiments ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. We use attention at a resolution of </span><math id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16\times 16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16\times 16</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and the encoder and decoder are symmetric. The total number of trainable parameters on the multilevel </span><math id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> -VAE is </span><math id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="148" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">148</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">148</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Million.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For implementing the non-linear diffusion model (</span><a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Non-linear Diffusion in Latent Space ‣ 4 Reversing the Information Loss ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">), we increase the U-Net’s output channels to </span><math id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and leave the rest of the architecture unmodified. As our diffusion model produces two outputs and is designed to model the noise at every time step along with a difference predictor (</span><a href="#S4.E17" title="In 4.2 Non-linear Diffusion in Latent Space ‣ 4 Reversing the Information Loss ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) we use more than </span><math id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="300" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">300</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">300</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Million parameters in our testing and report results with a network having </span><math id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="378" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">378</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">378</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p3.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Million trainable parameters.</span><a href="#A3.T6" title="In C.1.3 Unconditional Image Generation ‣ C.1 Details of Implementation ‣ Appendix C Details of experiments ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p3.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> lists the hyperparameters we used for training the unconditional diffusion models for all data sets. Next, we elaborate on the learned noise schedules.</span></p>
</div>
