<tr id="A3.T6.8.12" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T6.8.12.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:1.3pt;padding-bottom:1.3pt;">
<span id="A3.T6.8.12.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="A3.T6.8.12.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="A3.T6.8.12.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Iterations*</span></span>
</span></th>
<td id="A3.T6.8.12.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.3pt;padding-bottom:1.3pt;"><span id="A3.T6.8.12.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">120k</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.8.12.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.3pt;padding-bottom:1.3pt;"><span id="A3.T6.8.12.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">180k</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.8.12.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.3pt;padding-bottom:1.3pt;"><span id="A3.T6.8.12.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">300k</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T6.8.13" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T6.8.13.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:1.3pt;padding-bottom:1.3pt;">
<span id="A3.T6.8.13.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="A3.T6.8.13.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="A3.T6.8.13.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Learning Rate</span></span>
</span></th>
<td id="A3.T6.8.13.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:1.3pt;padding-bottom:1.3pt;"><span id="A3.T6.8.13.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">5.6e-5</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.8.13.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:1.3pt;padding-bottom:1.3pt;"><span id="A3.T6.8.13.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">4.4e-5</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.8.13.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:1.3pt;padding-bottom:1.3pt;"><span id="A3.T6.8.13.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">4.4e-5</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS3.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_paragraph" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Noise Schedule:</h5>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS3.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS3.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">As elaborated in </span><a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Controlling Information Loss with 𝛽 ‣ 3 Multi-𝛽 Representation Learning ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> our method learns </span><math id="A3.SS1.SSS3.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> as a result of training the multi-</span><math id="A3.SS1.SSS3.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> VAE which is the first stage of training irrespective of the dataset. The </span><math id="A3.SS1.SSS3.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.Px1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> obtained at the termination of this first stage of training is dependent on the choice of schedules of </span><math id="A3.SS1.SSS3.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.Px1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> which control the coefficients of </span><em id="A3.SS1.SSS3.Px1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">reconstruction term</em><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.Px1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><em id="A3.SS1.SSS3.Px1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">regularisation term</em><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.Px1.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> in </span><a href="#S3.E4" title="In 3.1 Conditional Multi-level 𝛽-VAE ‣ 3 Multi-𝛽 Representation Learning ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.Px1.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. In the following plot, we present two examples of learned noise schedules using empirically determined </span><math id="A3.SS1.SSS3.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.Px1.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> schedules and contrast it with a linear noise schedule.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F3" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2507.06613v1/noise_beta.svg" id="A3.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:238/181;" width="238" height="181"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F3.22" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 3</span>: </span><span id="A3.F3.23" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Examples of preferable noise schedules in our framework. These noise schedules have been used for learning non-linear diffusion models in <a href="#S6.T3" title="In 6.2 Evaluating Generation Quality ‣ 6 Experiments ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. While CelebAHQ <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bibx20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Karras et al., 2018</a>)</cite> trains better with <span id="A3.F3.23.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Sched 1</span>, both FFHQ <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bibx23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Karras et al., 2019</a>)</cite> and LSUN-Bedrooms<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bibx51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yu et al., 2015</a>)</cite> train better with <span id="A3.F3.23.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Sched 2</span>.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS3.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS3.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The training of the non-linear diffusion model is sensitive to the setting of this schedule, for instance, none of our models work well for a schedule that grows sub-linearly for </span><math id="A3.SS1.SSS3.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&lt;0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&lt;0.5</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.Px1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. The sudden increment in noise close to </span><math id="A3.SS1.SSS3.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.Px1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> does not affect the model’s performance negatively. Such a simga schedule is obtained by following a sinusoidal schedule for </span><math id="A3.SS1.SSS3.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS1.SSS3.Px1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. The exact form of our schedule is present in the shared code.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Latent manipulation and interpolation</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.2" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_middle" style="width:310.5pt;">
        
<figure id="algorithm4" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 4</span> </span>Manipulate images with given direction</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm4.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm4.6.1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Input :</span><span id="algorithm4.6.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Multi-</span><math id="algorithm4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm4.6.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> VAE </span><math id="algorithm4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{\theta},\bm{\phi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝜽</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{\theta},\bm{\phi})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm4.6.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, Non-linear diffusion model </span><math id="algorithm4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{\epsilon}_{\psi},\bm{\Delta}_{\psi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚫</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{\epsilon}_{\psi},\bm{\Delta}_{\psi})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm4.6.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, an image </span><math id="algorithm4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm4.6.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, latent direction </span><math id="algorithm4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝜹</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm4.6.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, manipulation factor </span><math id="algorithm4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm4.6.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, time step </span><math id="algorithm4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\beta</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.6.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Output :</span><span id="algorithm4.6.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Manipulated image </span><math id="algorithm4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{\mathrm{man}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">man</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{\mathrm{man}}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.6.3" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.6.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.6.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1</span></span>
              <span id="algorithm4.6.3.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Encode the image as </span><math id="algorithm4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}_{\beta}=f_{\phi}(\bm{x},\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}_{\beta}=f_{\phi}(\bm{x},\beta)</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.6.4" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.6.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.6.4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2</span></span>
              <span id="algorithm4.6.4.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Add the perturbation to the encoded latent </span><math id="algorithm4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{z}}_{\beta}=\bm{z}+\alpha\bm{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝜹</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{z}}_{\beta}=\bm{z}+\alpha\bm{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.6.5" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.6.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.6.5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">3</span></span>
              <span id="algorithm4.6.5.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Denoise </span><math id="algorithm4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{z}}_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{z}}_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm4.6.5.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> back to </span><math id="algorithm4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm4.6.5.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> using diffusion model </span><math id="algorithm4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{\epsilon}_{\psi},\bm{\Delta}_{\psi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚫</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{\epsilon}_{\psi},\bm{\Delta}_{\psi})</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.6.6" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.6.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.6.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">4</span></span>
              <span id="algorithm4.6.6.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Decode </span><math id="algorithm4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{z}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{z}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm4.6.6.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> as </span><math id="algorithm4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{\mathrm{man}}=g_{\theta}(\tilde{\bm{z}}_{0},\beta=0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">man</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">g</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{\mathrm{man}}=g_{\theta}(\tilde{\bm{z}}_{0},\beta=0)</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.6.7" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.6.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.6.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">5</span></span>
              <span id="algorithm4.6.7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">return</span><span id="algorithm4.6.7.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><math id="algorithm4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{\mathrm{man}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">man</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{\mathrm{man}}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.6.8" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
</div>
</figure>
        
<figure id="algorithm5" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 5</span> </span>Interpolate a pair of images</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm5.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm5.6.1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm5.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Input :</span><span id="algorithm5.6.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Multi-</span><math id="algorithm5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm5.6.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> VAE </span><math id="algorithm5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{\theta},\bm{\phi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝜽</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{\theta},\bm{\phi})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm5.6.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, Non-linear diffusion model </span><math id="algorithm5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{\epsilon}_{\psi},\bm{\Delta}_{\psi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚫</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{\epsilon}_{\psi},\bm{\Delta}_{\psi})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm5.6.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, images </span><math id="algorithm5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm5.6.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><math id="algorithm5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm5.6.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, interpolation factor </span><math id="algorithm5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm5.6.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, target dimensions to interpolate </span><math id="algorithm5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm5.6.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, time step </span><math id="algorithm5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\beta</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm5.6.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm5.6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Output :</span><span id="algorithm5.6.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Interpolated image </span><math id="algorithm5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{\mathrm{int}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">int</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{\mathrm{int}}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm5.6.3" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm5.6.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm5.6.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1</span></span>
              <span id="algorithm5.6.3.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Encode the images as </span><math id="algorithm5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}_{\beta,1}=f_{\phi}(\bm{x}_{1},\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}_{\beta,1}=f_{\phi}(\bm{x}_{1},\beta)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm5.6.3.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><math id="algorithm5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}_{\beta,2}=f_{\phi}(\bm{x}_{2},\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}_{\beta,2}=f_{\phi}(\bm{x}_{2},\beta)</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm5.6.4" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm5.6.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm5.6.4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2</span></span>
              <span id="algorithm5.6.4.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Initialize the latent variable as </span><math id="algorithm5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{z}}_{\beta}=\bm{z}_{\beta,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{z}}_{\beta}=\bm{z}_{\beta,1}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm5.6.5" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm5.6.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm5.6.5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">3</span></span>
              <span id="algorithm5.6.5.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Interpolate latent variables as </span><math id="algorithm5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{z}}_{\beta}[j]=\texttt{Slerp}(\bm{z}_{\beta,1}[j],\bm{z}_{\beta,2}[j],\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">Slerp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{z}}_{\beta}[j]=\texttt{Slerp}(\bm{z}_{\beta,1}[j],\bm{z}_{\beta,2}[j],\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm5.6.5.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> for </span><math id="algorithm5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm5.6.6" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm5.6.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm5.6.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">4</span></span>
              <span id="algorithm5.6.6.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Denoise </span><math id="algorithm5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{z}}_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{z}}_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm5.6.6.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> back to </span><math id="algorithm5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm5.6.6.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> using diffusion model </span><math id="algorithm5.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{\epsilon}_{\psi},\bm{\Delta}_{\psi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚫</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{\epsilon}_{\psi},\bm{\Delta}_{\psi})</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm5.6.7" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm5.6.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm5.6.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">5</span></span>
              <span id="algorithm5.6.7.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Decode </span><math id="algorithm5.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{z}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{z}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm5.6.7.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> as </span><math id="algorithm5.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{\mathrm{int}}=g_{\theta}(\tilde{\bm{z}}_{0},\beta=0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">int</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">g</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{\mathrm{int}}=g_{\theta}(\tilde{\bm{z}}_{0},\beta=0)</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm5.6.8" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm5.6.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm5.6.8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">6</span></span>
              <span id="algorithm5.6.8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">return</span><span id="algorithm5.6.8.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><math id="algorithm5.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{\mathrm{int}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">int</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{\mathrm{int}}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm5.6.9" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
</div>
</figure>
      
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">In </span><a href="#S2.F1" title="In 2 Overview of 𝛽-VAE ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a><span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, we obtain high-fidelity manipulated images by following Algorithm </span><a href="#algorithm4" title="Algorithm 4 ‣ C.2 Latent manipulation and interpolation ‣ Appendix C Details of experiments ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a><span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. The candidates for the latent direction </span><math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝜹</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> are eigenvectors obtained via Principal Component Analysis (PCA) of a large set of latent embeddings. Algorithm </span><a href="#algorithm5" title="Algorithm 5 ‣ C.2 Latent manipulation and interpolation ‣ Appendix C Details of experiments ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a><span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> presents the pseudocode for interpolating between two images, with examples of the interpolated images shown in </span><a href="#A4.F7" title="In D.5 Exploring the Spectrum of Learned Latents ‣ Appendix D Additional Results ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a><span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. We begin by producing an interpolated encoding at a time step </span><math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> using an interpolation coefficient </span><math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to control the mixing between </span><math id="A3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><math id="A3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Both algorithms require a trained multi-</span><math id="A3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> VAE and the corresponding nonlinear diffusion model to generate high-fidelity images.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Additional Results</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This section presents additional results from applying our method to high-quality image datasets. In </span><a href="#A4.SS1" title="D.1 Orthogonality of our method and DisCo ‣ Appendix D Additional Results ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a><span id="A4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, we demonstrate that our approach is complementary to learning-free methods by comparing it with DisCo </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="A4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bibx38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ren et al., 2022</a><span id="A4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="A4.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. In </span><a href="#A4.SS2" title="D.2 The relationship between 𝛽 and disentanglement ‣ Appendix D Additional Results ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a><span id="A4.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, we investigate the relationship between disentanglement and the value of </span><math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. In </span><a href="#A4.SS3" title="D.3 Multi-𝛽 VAE Reconstructions ‣ Appendix D Additional Results ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a><span id="A4.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, we show additional reconstructions generated by the multi-</span><math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> VAE. </span><a href="#A4.SS4" title="D.4 Generated Samples from Noise ‣ Appendix D Additional Results ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.4</span></a><span id="A4.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> includes samples generated by our model for qualitative evaluation, supporting the results presented in </span><a href="#S6.T3" title="In 6.2 Evaluating Generation Quality ‣ 6 Experiments ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a><span id="A4.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and confirming that our model can function as a standalone generative model. Furthermore, </span><a href="#A4.F8" title="In D.5 Exploring the Spectrum of Learned Latents ‣ Appendix D Additional Results ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a><span id="A4.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> explores the spectrum of learned latent representations through latent interpolation and attribute editing.</span></p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Orthogonality of our method and DisCo</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, we follow the same experimental setup as <a href="#S6.SS1.SSS2" title="6.1.2 Common Benchmark with Toy Datasets ‣ 6.1 Evaluating Disentanglement ‣ 6 Experiments ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1.2</span></a>.
As shown in <a href="#A4.T7" title="In D.1 Orthogonality of our method and DisCo ‣ Appendix D Additional Results ‣ Denoising Multi-𝛽 VAE: Representation Learning for Disentanglement and Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, our multi-<math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> VAE achieves better disentanglement performance compared to DisCo applied to standard VAE. Furthermore, DisCo consistently performs best when applied to multi-<math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> VAE, indicating that DisCo and our approach are complementary. Notably, while DisCo significantly improves standard VAE’s performance, its impact on multi-<math id="A4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> VAE is relatively marginal, suggesting that our model’s latent space is already well-disentangled.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T7" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A4.T7.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 7</span>: </span><span id="A4.T7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
Disentanglement results. The experimental setup follows Section 6.1, using identical VAE architectures for all methods.
</span></figcaption>
